 inelastic/elastic =  1.000: distortion surviving from T_max = 2, 5, 10 MeV -> [0. 0. 0.]
 inelastic/elastic =  0.100: distortion surviving from T_max = 2, 5, 10 MeV -> [0.129 0.    0.   ]
 inelastic/elastic =  0.010: distortion surviving from T_max = 2, 5, 10 MeV -> [0.792 0.003 0.   ]
 inelastic/elastic =  0.001: distortion surviving from T_max = 2, 5, 10 MeV -> [0.976 0.554 0.004]
elastic scattering alone never changes a group's population: the spectrum is an exact pocket against it;
only the slower inelastic exchange erases it, so survival is set by that ratio, not by how hot the bath is.
